mmit_sha":"e8cccb2230ceaeab779647ffdcd88f4322b0cca2","position":"1787070826261887001-0e583669-376d-4c34-ad49-2edb5961f873"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f0fa059ddad4f959ce080aa16f72c685b23226881fdae7a3834207dd697b729d","event_uuid":"b134c1a3-8071-4be4-963b-fd21465bb4c1","position":{"commit_sha":"856f862d7839f55066cc44b6415d2a3f57878e9c","position":"1787070832138663001-b134c1a3-8071-4be4-963b-fd21465bb4c1"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787069641619693001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a2fed048-e78c-45a5-b18f-acc8d72abc68","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"e499-704e-fa13-4916"},{"link_uuid":"87a9e66e-67ef-4c4f-bb3b-2800aecb6cc6","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"448e-3c6d-9e01-45cc"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nS2 makes runtime parsing and committed package help share one argparse source, but downstream consumers can still recreate drift. Today `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` regex-parses the intercept ladder and owns a curated command table; help/exit-code tests rebuild route sets; clean-wheel CI does not exercise every parser-derived artifact or lazy-reference contract.\n\n## Approach\nMake registries and S2-generated parser artifacts the only enumerable syntax inputs for documentation and distribution checks.\n\n- Generate every command syntax/options section in `docs/cli-reference.md` from registry enumeration plus the exact committed package-help bytes proven current by `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check`.\n- Delete `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS`, source regex parsing, and any hand-maintained command/usage/option census.\n- Keep cross-command rationale and examples editorial, but structurally separate from generated syntax sections. A deterministic lint rejects editorial `Usage:`/option-table authorities and validates referenced top-level spellings against the route registry; parser artifacts remain authoritative on disagreement.\n- Replace manual route unions in overview/help/argparse/exit-code tests with canonical/exact/compatibility/hidden/retired registry enumeration.\n- Extend the local-capable optionality harness and `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` clean-wheel lane to build a no-extras wheel, run `gen_cli_help.py --check` and `gen_cli_reference.py --check`, render every approved help form in a fresh directory, and assert no operation/config/store/handler/heavy import.\n- Add a full-runtime-extra contract that resolves every lazy handler/parser/selector reference and validates every capability-to-extra mapping without executing command logic.\n- Smoke-test `rebar-mcp` separately. Every CI check must have the same repository-local command for non-GitHub environments.\n\nRegistry validation covers route/resource census. S2's generator covers parser/artifact drift. Full-extra validation covers lazy-reference typos. No source grep substitutes for observable help/dispatch behavior.\n\n## Compatibility and Rollback\nDerived compatibility exports remain through S6. Reference syntax changes only with reviewed parser/generated-help changes; editorial prose may improve without redefining grammar. Reverting docs/generator/test/CI changes leaves runtime and stored data untouched.\n\n## Testing\nUse byte regeneration checks, generator unit tests, real clean-wheel subprocesses, import blockers, and full-extra symbol resolution. Negative fixtures include a parser/help byte drift, unresolved parser/handler, stray resource, omitted route, hidden alias leakage, retired token, editorial syntax table, unknown prose spelling, and heavy optional import. Prove each test collects and executes under a gating local/CI command.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check` and `scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check` prove the complete reference syntax/options derive from runtime-used parser artifacts and are byte-current.\n- [ ] No source regex, `INTERCEPT_COMMANDS`, manual command-description census, or editorial usage/option table remains.\n- [ ] Overview/help/exit-code tests enumerate all route classes from the registry rather than reconstructing policy sets.\n- [ ] A clean no-extras wheel renders every approved help form with exact bytes and no operation/config/store/parser/handler/heavy-import effect.\n- [ ] The full-extra contract resolves every handler/parser/selector and capability-to-extra reference without command execution.\n- [ ] Editorial examples/rationale are structurally separate, registry-linted for top-level spellings, and never override generated syntax.\n- [ ] The same commands run locally and in portable CI, with `rebar-mcp` tested as a separate entry point.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Generate syntax sections from registry and parser-derived package help; retain only separated editorial prose."},{"path":"docs/cli-reference.md","reason":"Regenerated complete parser-derived CLI reference."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py","reason":"Generator, editorial separation/lint, and parser-artifact drift tests."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py","reason":"Registry-enumerated overview and route-class coverage."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/facades/test_cli_argparse.py","reason":"Registry-enumerated help and route contracts."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py","reason":"Registry-enumerated exit-code documentation coverage."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py","reason":"Clean-wheel every-help-form and import/store/config contract."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_cli_registry_full_extra.py","reason":"Full-extra handler/parser/selector/capability reference resolution."},{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"Invoke portable lean-wheel, generator, full-extra, and MCP contracts."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","448e-3c6d-9e01-45cc"],["depends_on","e499-704e-fa13-4916"],["parent","09ae-e827-1cac-452d"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"09ae-e827-1cac-452d","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["rp05","cli"],"ticket_id":"6755-d43c-b962-45a8","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-05 S5 — Derive CLI reference and distribution contracts from the registries","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/gen_cli_help.py --check && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/gen_cli_reference.py --check && env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py tests/interfaces/contracts/test_help_overview_coverage.py tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_exit_codes_doc_conformance.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC3","dd_text":"Parser-help and CLI-reference generation plus registry-enumerated consumers"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/interfaces/contracts/test_cli_registry_distribution.py","dd_id":"AC4","dd_text":"Clean no-extras wheel exact help/import/store/config contract"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_cli_registry_full_extra.py tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp.py","dd_id":"AC5-AC7","dd_text":"Full-extra lazy refs, editorial lint, portable CI parity, and separate MCP entrypoint"}]},"source_event_uuids":["aecda70d-c857-42f9-89fa-39ee70907b26","5866d21d-8d33-4ea0-9610-cb2f194f4c3c","af82f0f9-b1d7-43a6-8b03-4d5634317bd0","a2fed048-e78c-45a5-b18f-acc8d72abc68","87a9e66e-67ef-4c4f-bb3b-2800aecb6cc6","c3cacb79-adfe-4b76-9fd5-94818a54f311","0e583669-376d-4c34-ad49-2edb5961f873","b134c1a3-8071-4be4-963b-fd21465bb4c1"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787076418195717996,"uuid":"2ba40dc3-8a8c-4c37-b017-d01b1c666018"}